<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:17Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Live: Saudi Arabia reports Aramco building hit and four wounded in Houthi missile attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5841853aba76070ec4b0bfa55ecbe9c4e8cce80f9b45c2a13f943af16d22f39a</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T03:39:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261014-live-saudi-arabia-reports-aramco-building-hit-and-four-wounded-in-houthi-missile-attacks" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia reported damage to an Aramco building in Dhahran and four people wounded in Riyadh on Wednesday, after the kingdom intercepted Houthi missiles targeting the capital. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Trump asks US ambassador to Greece Kimberly Guilfoyle to resign over allegations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ad613bb8162e8ebd8746b32cb671daacfaf216aeda7f8f999a0bd87c86b4c82d</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T03:23:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-trump-asks-us-ambassador-to-greece-kimberly-guilfoyle-to-resign-over-allegations" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump asked US ambassador to Greece Kimberly Guilfoyle to resign on Tuesday after reports alleged she sought $100,000 from a Trump supporter to pay personal credit card debt and accepted luxury trips and hotel stays from wealthy Greek businessmen. Guilfoyle denied wrongdoing and vowed to defend her reputation.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Kyiv power plant hit by Russian missile without warning from allies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe273064d2fc9f53ab16957182b9cdf4d17bc5c7df4603ac485725dd485172b5</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T00:41:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-kyiv-power-plant-hit-by-russian-missile-without-warning-from-allies" /><summary type="html">Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky said Tuesday that a Russian ballistic missile struck a Kyiv power plant without advance warning from Western allies, killing at least two people and wounding around 20. The attack came days after US President Donald Trump announced an energy ceasefire between Moscow and Kyiv, raising questions over efforts to halt strikes on critical infrastructure.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Arsenal thrash Lille as Atletico Madrid beat Manchester United</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd52b65952bf11b3f94317267d104c4650ca958873a0798f19ce904015d55245</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T21:59:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20261013-arsenal-thrash-lille-as-atletico-madrid-beat-manchester-united" /><summary type="html">Arsenal scored three goals in seven second-half minutes on Tuesday to beat Lille 3-0 and maintain their perfect Champions League start, while Atletico Madrid defeated Manchester United 2-0 to deepen the pressure on Michael Carrick. Bayern Munich were held to a shock 3-3 draw by Norway’s Viking after Michael Olise was sent off.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo has cancerous growth removed in lung operation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ebb1a93aae8f4109441aa3c0c3ed1f4e46132faebd97ad50523ab47b3d239ba</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T21:23:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/pope-leo-has-cancerous-growth-removed-in-lung-operation" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV had a cancerous growth removed from his right lung in a 90-minute operation on Tuesday and "woke up normally" after the procedure, the Vatican said. A Vatican source said further tests were being carried out to determine if the cancer had spread. "To ensure the procedure was radical, the lower lobe of the right lung was removed," the Vatican said in a statement. FRANCE 24's Seema Gupta reports from Rome.</summary></entry><entry><title>China is bringing car production to EU</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a589c892c2af75e2a7b8f501b6622831fb60ce9cecc9c9e4eb531f30be124368</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T21:23:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261013-china-is-bringing-car-production-to-eu" /><summary type="html">China has moved from exporting cars to bringing entire auto industry ecosystems, building up production capacity in Europe and boosting partnerships with local companies. Arthur D. Little's automotive expert Philipp Seidel tells France 24 that while tariffs and quotas can buy time, EU carmakers must improve their own competitiveness and not become too dependent on Chinese suppliers. But first, we look at the latest IMF global growth forecast and warning about rising debt.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Supermarket fridge hacking attacks due to lack of basic cybersecurity measures, expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e244570ef66496f610a67a4a140ba29f5e6f13991474b364c1101b92dc81f42f</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T21:06:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261013-supermarket-fridge-hacking-attacks-due-to-lack-of-basic-cybersecurity-measures-expert-says" /><summary type="html">French investigators on Tuesday ​were hunting the hackers who seized control of cooling units at hundreds of supermarkets in a cyberattack that underlined the vulnerabilities of connected systems, with no group publicly claiming responsibility. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Marta Rybczynska, cybersecurity expert at Ygreky. She says that basic measures like regularly updating software or passwords are essential to prevent hacking attacks.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Supermarket fridge hacking attacks due to lack of basic cybersecurity measures, expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d965e877ac85743d7fd2da3f132b58a0785b098dfea8436222d32c611a35a4af</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T21:05:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/supermarket-fridge-hacking-attacks-due-to-lack-of-basic-cybersecurity-measures-expert-says" /><summary type="html">French investigators on Tuesday ​were hunting the hackers who seized control of cooling units at hundreds of supermarkets in a cyberattack that underlined the vulnerabilities of connected systems, with no group publicly claiming responsibility. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Marta Rybczynska, cybersecurity expert at Ygreky. She says that basic measures like regularly updating software or passwords are essential to prevent hacking attacks.</summary></entry><entry><title>Have Ukrainian strikes on Yandex data centres hit Russian online disinformation?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2dd6714f807d0b1e4fe361ca05f1e45a59ed4311603c90c8a27c9841d8095fe7</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T20:59:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261013-have-ukrainian-strikes-on-yandex-data-centres-hit-russian-online-disinformation" /><summary type="html">After recent Ukrainian bombings of Russian data centres belonging to Yandex, internet users claim to have noticed a sharp reduction in pro-Russian and far-right populist social media content. They suggest the reduction is a direct result of the strikes cutting off Russian disinformation "bots". We examine the claim in this edition of Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Surgery on Pope Leo's cancerous lung nodule went well, Vatican says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:797d3a88dd472f2a7e7696a9cf6f7437659d48eb86503dc43856275c767b1473</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T20:44:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-what-we-know-about-pope-leo-xiv-planned-lung-operation-this-week--42462f7a7f54.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-what-we-know-about-pope-leo-xiv-planned-lung-operation-this-week" /></entry><entry><title>Former gang leader sentenced to minimum 40 years for Tupac killing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c2260fae17387a112443a6e1ca2777e0927da3778486d149069b54854b0fa54</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T20:33:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/former-gang-leader-sentenced-to-minimum-40-years-for-tupac-killing--2d8cf39e1327.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/former-gang-leader-sentenced-to-minimum-40-years-for-tupac-killing" /><summary type="html">Duane Davis, the former Los Angeles gang leader who boasted in books and interviews of his involvement in the killing of rapper Tupac Shakur, only to deny it when he came to trial, was sentenced to a minimum 40 years in prison on Tuesday. FRANCE 24's Wassim Cornet reports from Los Angeles.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump asks Greece ambassador to resign amid ethics scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f2d20fea6d0d391a8b6cfd1ad04235e8fa1de2087407dfc133a750c61c919a1b</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T20:29:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-asks-greece-ambassador-to-resign-amid-ethics-scandal--24c18b5f16df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-asks-greece-ambassador-to-resign-amid-ethics-scandal" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump's administration has asked his ambassador to Greece Kimberly Guilfoyle to resign, the White House said Tuesday, amid allegations that she sought money from a Trump supporter and accepted lavish hospitality from wealthy Greek businessmen. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson reports from Washington.</summary></entry><entry><title>Kabila launches new coalition with M23</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:daaeee50071f995a31f907a93a7140f4ead0fc45e7dd118092439c39268b4cc8</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T20:21:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/kabila-launches-new-coalition-with-m23--ed60166777a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kabila-launches-new-coalition-with-m23" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, Joseph Kabila has been named leader of a new rebel coalition, vowing to topple the government. Also, Africa's largest ever IPO has been extended. And Formula ⁠1 ⁠will return to ⁠Africa in ​the early 2030s, once a new circuit is built in Rwanda.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>French MPs pass sweeping bill to combat sexual and gender-based violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d32ee6a43903ea3a1a51346cf89afd23a0b9d66089336d249a7795f88aaebfb</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T20:03:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-mps-pass-sweeping-bill-to-combat-sexual-and-gender-based-violence--5235867145cb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-mps-pass-sweeping-bill-to-combat-sexual-and-gender-based-violence" /><summary type="html">The National Assembly overwhelmingly passed the so-called “comprehensive” bill against sexist and sexual violence on Tuesday. The focus now shifts to the more conservative Senate, with the bill’s supporters fearing that its main advances could be watered down, even though the government insists it will act as guarantor of the bill’s ambition. Sponsored in the Assembly by eight political groups, from the Communists to Les Républicains (LR), the text was adopted by 503 votes to 0. Only the LFI (La France Insoumise) deputies abstained, denouncing in particular the removal of measures aimed at protecting foreign women. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Former gang leader sentenced to 40 years to life for Tupac Shakur murder</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa305d8f030ed53db827d79f7626e6685e609a25e458797878c78c8c38e03219</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T19:57:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261013-former-gang-leader-sentenced-to-40-years-to-life-for-tupac-shakur-murder--2d6357adbe6e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261013-former-gang-leader-sentenced-to-40-years-to-life-for-tupac-shakur-murder" /><summary type="html">Duane “Keffe D” Davis, the former Los Angeles gang leader who boasted in books and interviews of his involvement in the killing of rapper Tupac Shakur, only to deny it when he came to trial, was sentenced to a minimum 40 years in prison on Tuesday.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>France's youth undergoing 'a crisis of hope'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25964c11e88abe5fff85da1dfe87715d40c2d6a76060f0e6db618527e9432e06</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T19:33:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-s-youth-undergoing-a-crisis-of-hope--deece93fa1c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-s-youth-undergoing-a-crisis-of-hope" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of people joined rallies across France on Tuesday to support protesting high school students, boosting a movement that poses a major challenge to President Emmanuel Macron as his term in office winds down. Some 161,500 people turned out, according to the interior ministry -- more than double the 71,500 it gave for the last nationwide demonstrations on Thursday last week. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Andrew Smith, Lecturer in Liberal Arts at Queen Mary's London, says that France's youth is undergoing "a crisis of hope" which is pushing "the anger and the sense that something has to change".</summary></entry><entry><title>Ceuta an 'inalienable' part of Spain, king says on key visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e432308b71dea07a575317a1944af565d282dc719286e246a792372154e7bada</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T19:06:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ceuta-an-inalienable-part-of-spain-king-says-on-key-visit--84d6778d9333.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ceuta-an-inalienable-part-of-spain-king-says-on-key-visit" /><summary type="html">King Felipe VI on Tuesday said Ceuta and Melilla were "an inalienable part" of Spain as he made a landmark visit to the north African territories claimed by neighbouring Morocco. "Ceuta and Melilla are an inalienable part of the political and national reality that is Spain. The sovereignty and territorial integrity of our country are not negotiable," Felipe said. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tens of thousands rally across France as high school protests gather strength</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f879d82ac35ef7f89cdf2a4adf9a0c15d5a1ab05aae4f0ddd30b74d86c90e1e1</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T18:21:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261013-tens-of-thousands-rally-across-france-as-high-school-protests-gather-strength--7c387a32d594.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261013-tens-of-thousands-rally-across-france-as-high-school-protests-gather-strength" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of people rallied across France on Tuesday in support of protesting high school students, with unions putting turnout at 480,000, as anger over school conditions and alleged police violence fuels a growing movement challenging President Emmanuel Macron’s government ahead of planned cost-of-living demonstrations on Saturday.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>France's fed-up youth: Can presidential candidates connect with student movement?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:498a4e7f53bf6ce7182105bb27e8825fe1e69edaaea8cb93a86b8f2134a3c967</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T18:10:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261013-france-s-fed-up-youth-can-presidential-candidates-connect-with-student-movement--803e75a12ac2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261013-france-s-fed-up-youth-can-presidential-candidates-connect-with-student-movement" /><summary type="html">Will it be autumn recess to the rescue for a beleaguered French government? Ministers no doubt counting the days until Friday evening when the holidays start in hopes that an unexpected student movement disappears as quickly as it materialized. A movement sparked three weeks ago by deteriorating conditions in a Paris area high school may take a leave of absence… but what about demands for a generation that feels left behind by cost cutting? Only one party’s sided vocally with the students since the very start, Jean-Luc Mélenchon’s far-left France Unbowed.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>ISS amid global conflict: A rare bastion of 'scientific collaboration' between the East and West</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f33f0fd28e49de3e366ce76c9b6068cd936b0a1fb64bfd9d48fd8a20cc1d8ff</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T17:53:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261013-iss-amid-global-conflict-a-rare-bastion-of-scientific-collaboration-between-the-east-and-we--01170922784a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261013-iss-amid-global-conflict-a-rare-bastion-of-scientific-collaboration-between-the-east-and-west" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Alban Guyomarc'h, Researcher in Space Geopolitics at Paris's École Normale Supérieure School of Higher Learning. As a new era of space rivalry unfolds, the International Space Station remains one of the last bastions of cooperation between geopolitical adversaries. For Guyomarc'h, the latest ISS mission is more than a remarkable technological achievement. "It's one of the rare collaboration spaces we still have today in a very conflictual era".</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Digital distrust and polarisation: 'We need to get back to engaging with one another as a society'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af269b75915f3b9defd817a7a838433a31a5f0387982d931c03d6068337b0463</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T17:39:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261013-digital-distrust-and-polarisation-we-need-to-get-back-to-engaging-with-one-another-as-a-soc--34372d50a6d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261013-digital-distrust-and-polarisation-we-need-to-get-back-to-engaging-with-one-another-as-a-society" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Valdemar Osted, partner and head of technology at Danish digital consultancy Common Consultancy. Can the fear of disinformation become as dangerous to democracy as disinformation itself? Osted challenges widely circulated claims that attacks on Russian data centres have triggered a sudden collapse in online engagement among supporters of Donald Trump and Germany's far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD). Drawing on social media monitoring and research into inauthentic behaviour, Osted reports finding no unusual decline in Facebook interactions following the attacks.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Syria: Israeli army accused of arbitrary arrests and detention</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f8910dcfe91bffb17df4500a7e767434ab05429527ed81ea65a7375cb9e4504b</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T17:28:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261013-syria-israeli-army-accused-arbitrary-arrests-detention--ad59aa39dde2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261013-syria-israeli-army-accused-arbitrary-arrests-detention" /><summary type="html">The Israeli army has arrested more than 200 people in southern Syria since the fall of Bashar al-Assad’s regime in December 2024, according to the Sijil Centre, which tracks Israeli activity in Syria. The Israeli military says it is targeting “suspected terrorists”. Witnesses, for their part, have denounced the arbitrary arrests, while former detainees and their loved ones have raised serious concerns over conditions in detention.</summary><category term="The Observers" /></entry><entry><title>Student protesters tell police to join them in Paris demonstrations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bfa1ae7c386223b1d0ffae35a0c54451c3e5a9f3ee29af948688969aecd2391d</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T17:04:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261013-student-protesters-tell-police-to-join-them-in-paris-demonstrations--c37f571fa6d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261013-student-protesters-tell-police-to-join-them-in-paris-demonstrations" /><summary type="html">As student-led protests in Paris came to a close on Tuesday, demonstrators chanted "join us, join us" to police officers, who took off their helmets to cheers of the crowd. "When police take off their helmets, it's a sign that things are getting calmer," said FRANCE 24 reporter Claire Paccalin. Broader demonstrations are set to take place across France on Saturday over the cost of living, as well as further student protests, with the two potentially merging into a substantial movement. "But many of the young people I have spoken to today say they will not participate on Saturday," Paccalin said.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: French students ‘not giving up the fight’ as 480,000 join new day of school protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9651669e2a19f3f532911947e0199e56e92b4f6094c180aca2742ad2de7bcbf5</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T16:16:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-live-france-braces-for-fresh-nationwide-protests-over-school-conditions--ed166873d347.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-live-france-braces-for-fresh-nationwide-protests-over-school-conditions" /></entry></feed>
